==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*siipi}}, possibly a {{der|fi|bat}} loan. Cognates include {{cog|et|tiib}}, Northern {{cog|krl|siipi}}, Southern {{cog|krl|siivi}}, {{cog|liv|tībõz}}, {{cog|lud|siib}}, {{cog|vep|šib|šīb}}, {{cog|vro|siib}}, {{cog|vot|siipi}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-p}}

===Noun===
{{head|fi|noun}}

# [[wing]] {{gloss|animal appendage for flying}}
# [[wing]] {{gloss|airplane part}}
# [[wing]] {{gloss|part of building}}
# [[wing]] {{gloss|fraction of political movement}}
# [[sail]] {{gloss|blade of a windmill}}
# [[wing]], [[arm]] {{gloss|of a seine}}
# [[blade]] or a [[paddle]] of a [[water wheel]] or a [[paddlewheel]]
# [[blade]] of a [[turbine]] or a [[propeller]]
# [[mouldboard]] {{gloss|curved blade on a plough that serves to turn over the furrow}}
# [[flyer]] of a [[spinning wheel]]
# {{lb|fi|slang}} [[wing]] {{gloss|human hand}}

